{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py", "README.md"], "claim_kind": "decision_record", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "recorded_decision", "observation_id": "OBS-006", "origin": "recorded", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "a2d26673aa9122f441c92c4d1fe7662bfa6dceda98a862ae7136114f45a8cb8c", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "price_fact (module docstring)", "source_kind": "source", "uri": "agent_cost/aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "6b3236a0d35fcae635a102cf2e6dc6d5776002fe78354877d157f94a4e6f27f6", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "## What this measures, and what it doesn't", "source_kind": "spec", "uri": "README.md"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "b8bb860740f30fe6e1f78c9d63b1a696e7d57e1594a71972a2e640b390a97999", "statement": "Pricing an unknown-TTL cache write at the 5-minute rate as an explicit lower bound -- instead of guessing the more expensive 1-hour rate, or averaging the two -- is a deliberate design decision, recorded in both price_fact's own docstring and the README's \"What this measures\" section, so a reader of the output number knows it is a floor, not a best-effort midpoint.", "subject_refs": ["price_fact"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-02", "valid_at_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/readers/codex.py"], "claim_kind": "behavior", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "single_source_observation", "observation_id": "OBS-007", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "010ba51f52092ad01f1effd88f0ba084467b609dae4469ce41c797a1f080109b", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "parse_rollout_facts", "source_kind": "source", "uri": "agent_cost/readers/codex.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "4c674142ed03e31ec80d10a5e1a3da62c45c5b6a585702c4a554adef7a3b11e8", "statement": "The Codex CLI reader (parse_rollout_facts) never emits a cache_write_5m, cache_write_1h, or cache_write_unknown fact for any event -- it only ever constructs Fact objects with token_kind \"input_nocache\", \"cache_read\", or \"output\". This matches the README's claim that Codex exposes no cache-write signal at all, but is recorded here from a direct, single-pass static read of the reader module rather than from a test that asserts the negative (no test in tests/test_reader_codex.py checks that \"cache_write\" never appears in a fact's token_kind).", "subject_refs": ["parse_rollout_facts"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-02", "valid_at_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py"], "claim_kind": "behavior", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "execution_verified", "observation_id": "OBS-008", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "4fa19557fb67f561bd959564173e7f05ba63205d1871683f11d9ff521956b34a", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "test_price_fact_unknown_model_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "4fa19557fb67f561bd959564173e7f05ba63205d1871683f11d9ff521956b34a", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "test_price_fact_codex_cache_write_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "440f06b2791b2326117807aaf47ea8889dcf552efa482b8f2593a7bd79fc01fd", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b", "selector": "test_gpt_5_5_cache_write_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_rates.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "3a8b7caa77daf5bb647dafbb5343b34b5aadbd8cf3078ba08ab01168d34e497c", "statement": "price_fact() returns (None, \"unpriced\", None) -- never a guessed number -- both when the fact's model_key does not resolve against the catalog at all, and when the model resolves but the specific token-kind rate field for the covering rate period is None (e.g. OpenAI models carry no cache_write_5m rate at all, so a cache-write fact against gpt-5.5 is unpriced even though the model itself is known).", "subject_refs": ["price_fact"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-03", "valid_at_commit": "1c74d44903e67e1f65bb28a0b0d39443f48f657b"}
